@Output from AddContract:
The Add method adds an item to the ArrayList at the last possible position. We store the old count, add the new object using 
arrList.Add(x), get the new count and verify if the new count is greater than the old count.

```cs
int Old_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
int New_Ret = arrList.Add(x);
int New_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
Assert.IsTrue(New_arrList_Count > Old_arrList_Count);
```

```
@Output from RemoveContract:
The Remove method removes an object from ArrayList by providing an object. We store the old count, remove the object
using arrList.Remove(x), get the new count and check if the new count is less than the old count.

```cs
int Old_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
arrList.Remove(x);
int New_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
Assert.IsTrue(New_arrList_Count < Old_arrList_Count);
```

```
@Output from InsertContract:
The Insert method inserts an object into ArrayList at a particular index. We verify that the index is valid (<= Count and >= 0)
and then add the object and check if the object's index is inserted at (index)

```cs
AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);
arrList.Insert(index, x);
Assert.AreEqual(x, arrList[index]);
```

```
@Output from SetContract: 
The Set method modifies an object in ArrayList by providing the object to be changed, its index, and the replacement object. 
We verify that the index is valid (>= 0 and < Count) and replace the array object.

```cs
AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index >= 0 && index < arrList.Count);
arrList[index]=x;
Assert.AreEqual(x, arrList[index]);
```

```
@Output from GetContract:
The Get method retrieves an object from ArrayList by specifying the index. We first verify if ArrayList Count is valid 
(>=0 and < Count) and if the index actually contains the intended object.

```cs
AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index < arrList.Count && index >= 0);
Assert.AreEqual(x, arrList[index]);
```

```
@Output from ContainsContract: 
The Contains method checks whether an ArrayList contains a specific item. We test this by storing the old count, adding the
object, checking the new count and seeing if the object is still in the ArrayList after adding it.

```cs
int Old_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
arrList.Add(x);
int New_arrList_Count = arrList.Count;
Assert.IsTrue(New_arrList_Count > Old_arrList_Count && arrList.Contains(x));
```

```
@Output from IndexOfContract:
The IndexOf method returns the index of the first occurrence of a specific object in a ArrayList. First we add the object, then
get its index.

```cs
arrList.Add(x);
int Old_index = arrList.IndexOf(x);
Assert.IsTrue(Old_index >= 0);
```

```
@Output from LastIndexOfContract:
The LastIndexOf method returns the index of the last occurrence of a specific object in a ArrayList. We first add the object
to the ArrayList then get its index.

```cs
arrList.Add(x);
Assert.IsTrue(arrList.LastIndexOf(x) >= 0);
```

```
